Auchan is the most expensive, almost one-fifth underpriced Tesco
Hypermarkets in the Budaör Trading Triangle have maintained last year, on average a 16 percent increase in the price level, with the difference that there has not been an increase in VAT this year.
Napi Gazdaság Diary of Napi Gazdaság
Napi Gazdaság's usual Christmas consumer basket has risen an average of 16 per cent this year in the Budaörs Trading Triangle this year, but in all hypermarkets there was an increase of over a Thousand forints.
Since the prices of food supermarkets "flying out" already last December last year, the percentage due to an earlier high base did not show such a drought-increase.
However, it is certainly unfortunate for the consumer that what they could easily buy last year at a price of under nine thousand forints will not be bought now for even ten thousand.
Consumption Basket of the Daily Economy in examined hypermarkets exceeded the psychological threshold of ten thousand forints by at least 91 forints.
The highest basket price was 10 573 forints.
(In 2003 a consumer basket cost 6 800 forints.)
The price of Unica and live fish remained almost at last year's level, but cruel breasts, nuts and also poppy.
The prices of bread and flour corresponded to the data of the Central Statistical Office, although in Auchan we also found kilogram bread for 139 forints.
Competition didn't go with the price of the product below 200 forints.
Likewise, it was astonishing in this store that the price of a two-liter Coca Coke in a reversible bottle was under 200 forints, so even with a deposit the product cost only 257 forints.
Even so, according to the consumption bin of Napi Gazdaság Auchan this year it appeared to be the most expensive, while Cora appeared to be the cheapest.
According to our calculations, the prices figure-setting Napi Gazdaság increased the prices figure-of-the-yielder by 15 last year, while Tesco and Auchan have risen by about 18 per cent.
Compared to last year's highest and this year's lowest consumer basket values, the difference was 12 per cent, while an increase between last year's lowest and this year's highest was 21 per cent.
There was an increment on an average of 1 480 in forints.
The average price increase last year came to 1,206 forints, with prices being impacted by VAT growth last year.
It was this process that submersified the trade, department stores evidently failed to decide how large the price range should be determined for individual products, because they could not predict what effect the change in prices will have on consumption.
(While a tradesman plans the speed of circulation of the product poorly, it may lose a significant profit due to the price range adapted to the intensity of circulation.)
Due to VAT last year, the increase in the price of the consumer basket of Napi Gazdaság manifested itself so extremely that the price of the most-expensive basket was 1,720 forints higher than in 2006, while for the cheapest, the price difference was all 8,44 forints.
This year there was no extreme difference, the most expensive basket now cost 1,630 forints more than last year, and also the cheapest underperimilar 1,284 forints.
Comparing two Christmas seasons, catastropcial price growth came to light, in less than 20 months it underpertracted goods of daily consumption in hypermarkets by more than 30 per cent.
(This, among other things, does not uncompropriately definitively reaffirm the Central Statistical Office's data: in the case of several staple foods, an increase in prices exceeding 30 per cent within 12 months.
In addition to flour, for example, in the case of eggs.)
In the latter case, however, according to the consumption basket of the Daily Economy, it seems almost impossible, because the price level of the product, quite expensive already last year, showed a price increase of barely more than 10 per cent due to the basis even in the worst case.
Flour suppliers seem to take stronger positions than egg suppliers, they have managed to promote a drastic price increase in international chains as well.
Hyper-markets are not complaining, they are not complaining, they are still reporting on a good year.
According to our experience, the majority of customers in three visited stores are no longer interested in prices.
Quantities are bought, durable food is taken after salaries.
On mid-morning in all three supermarkets, long queues at check-ups were forming, as the number of visitors has skyrocketed.
However, as we know, the turnover is lower in the countryside, several international chains are complaining to research companies that sales lag behind their plans, not only in the case of food, but also in durable consumer goods.
In many places it is saved on disinfection products
More than a Thousand cases of infection were registered in hospitals this year mainly due to inappropriate anti-antibiotic use.
Hygienic conditions of hospitals, overcrowding of beds, congestion of staff stopping the diseases do not help, says the head of the National Epidemiological Center.
In many places it is also saved on disinfection products.
MRSA was recently diagnosed with an MRSA infection in St. John's trauma ward.
Antibiotic-resistant bacteriums have been discovered in a man who came to the hospital after a serious traffic accident.
The patient was isolated.
A similar infection occurred in the same place at the beginning of the year.
The patient was discharged home in a serious car accident, but not long after he had to come back with MRSA infection and, due to a bacterium located in his body, an important operation could not yet be carried out.
As of December 10 this year, 1,094 hospital infections caused by multi-presistant agents of the disease have been reported to the National Nesocomialis Surveillance system, Karolina Böröcz, head of the National Epidemiological Center.
This means that so many infections caused by multi-resistent agents of the disease have certainly been registered in hospitals, others are unfamiliar.
Nearly two-three (683) infections were caused by MRSA, or methicilin-oxacillin-resistant golden staphylococcus.
Staphylococcus auerus (SA) bacterium is worn by a third of people in the nose without causing the disease.
Infections caused by SA (e.g. cervical inflammation, inflammation of the tonsils, skin infection, early infection) respond well to antibiotics and can be treated well.
However, if antiquities are administered to an exaggerated or inappropriate manner, it develops a bacterium well-responsible to antibiotics that is very resolute to antiquities and which spreads rapidly in unappropriate hospital conditions.
Primarily, in the case of transiently or permanently malfunction of the immune system in patients with a weakened organism, low body weight or in patients during the years, it can cause serious hospital infections, such as an early infection or blood poisoning - sepsis.
According to St. John's Hospital Chief Physician, there is nothing special about MRSA infection, similar infections in hospitals belong to the daily practice.
"Infection must not be confused with an outbreak, MRSA isn't just there," Tibor Nyulasi said, "who the presence of the causative agent of the disease isn't being investigated."
Resolute antibiotics
"We is isolate these patients, the nursing staff treats them in rubber gloves and in a mask and we have the necessary anti-antibiotics for their treatment," Tibor Nyulasi said.
Patients admitted to the hospital are first examined to see if it is present in their MRSA organism, but the infection cannot always be avoided.
Choosing a Sample is not in voyage
The vast majority of hospital infections caused by MRSA could be avoided, but the current conditions and conditions in domestic hospitals are not favorable for the prevention and spread of multi-resistant disease agents, according to Karolina Böröcz.
Since this infection occurs characteristically in hospitals and homes for the elderly, hospital-received patients should incite and immediately isolate MRSA carriers.
The collection of microbiological samples, however, is not in voyage in Hungarian hospitals.
This also plays a stance that the National Health Insurance Fund does not finance these examinations.
Most cases are thus uncovered if the patient suffers from a perceptible MRSA infection, the head of the Epidemiological Center said.
The European Union has appropriate anti-Citifest recommendations for appropriate anti-treatment in human medicine and there are also domestic guidelines for the treatment of individual infections, citors.
It is necessary to strive to ensure that antibiotic therapy is targeted, or microbiological examinations should be carried out in order to prevent the development of drug resistency, but even hospitals in all cases do not comply.
Microbiological sampling is even more rare for basic or out-patient treatment, Karolina Böröcz said.
Responsible for disinfectance
According to scientific Evidence, MRSA disseminates among patients most often through medical personnel.
That's why washing hands and the use of gloves and masks play a very important role, but there are also serious deficiencies in hospitals.
MRSA is transmitted by droplet infection even by contact, but it is not always possible to isolate the infected patients under the conditions of domestic hospitals.
On the contrary, the rooms are often overcrowded, the beds are often very close to each other, albeit from an epidemiological point of view, patients should be at least 1.5 meters apart.
As Karolina Böröcz noted, unfortunately, we can also meet the fact that in hospitals that are in an unfavorable material situation, there are few caregivers on disinfectancies, caregivers there are a lot and a lot of patients, which increases the chances of infection.
Karolina Böröcz said there is a result where the necessary protective measures are followed, similar infections demonstratively less, or the further spread of the causative agent of the disease can be halted.
Governance against MRSA
Treasure of MRSA infection poses a huge expense for health insurers, which is why it is being dealt with everywhere.
For example, in England, the government has drafted a MRSA prevention program, or a reduction in its incidence.
It seems that the program is successful, according to the published MRSA infections in England show a decreasing tendency.
The European Centre for Disease Prevention (ECDC) classifies the prevention of multi-resistent disease-resisting agents (which also include MRSA) or hospital-inflammers, caused by these disease-reducing agents.
