There's going to be a giant strike
The Association of Trade Unions of the Liga, respectively the Nationwide Union of Workers' Councils (MoSZ), will on Friday create its striking commission to coordinate Monday's unrestricted strike.
There will be a Protest public rally on Saturday, Monday - on the day of the final vote on the Health Insurance Act - work will be halted.
The action will certainly inflict serious disruptions in traffic, as rail transport is almost completely halted, and within 13 a.m. employees of the Budapest transport company (BKV) will also go on strike.
On Friday afternoon, the Liga association will acquaint themselves with the Nation-State Workers' Council Association with the details of a jointly organized Monday's strike.
There will also be a strike committee of the LEAGUE - MOSZ, which will coordinate Monday's action.
There will be a protest public rally on Saturday, and from Monday, unions joining the strike will halt work indefinitely, unless there is an agreement with the government.
This means there has not been a set deadline for an end to the strike, which will begin on the day of the parliamentary vote on the Health Insurance Act.
In the end, if Parliament does not adopt the Health Insurance Act, the unions will immediately withdraw the call for the strike.
However, if the legislation is voted on, strike commissions will come together to decide on the next course of action.
According to Monday's agenda for the meeting of Parliament, it is also possible that the Health Insurance Act will not be voted on until late in the evening or at night.
Due to the start-up strike on Monday, it is possible to count on serious traffic interruptions: on the railway the work will be halted for an indefinite period of time, in the morning it is possible to halt a part of Budapest public transport and more than a half by Volán.
At the same time, in many parts of the country there will also be the closure half of the runway.
Numerous trade unions and civil organizations, whose list is constantly being updated on the Ligoa association's website.
Some organizations announced an indefinition strike, while others declared a temporary cessation of work.
Until Thursday afternoon, the Hungarian State Railways (MÁV) and the Independent Trade Union of Railway Employees (VDSZSZ) were not even able to agree on sufficient services, while at the beginning of the Christmas holidays more and more and more people are traveling by rail.
According to previous reports, the start of operation will go on strike at the BKV, from 7 a.m. to 9 a.m. at Budapest Airport, a four-hour strike will be organized by the Union of Workers in the LIGA Entergable Energy Industry, the Union of Educators and the Democratic Trade Union of Educators have called for a 2- and a 2-8-hour graduation.
The Union of Hungarian Physicians will go on strike alternately all over the country, the Democratic Trade Union of Workers in Health Care Workers and in the Social (EDDSZ), belonging to the Co-operation Forum of Trade Unions (SZEF), is holding a two-hour warning strike.
The most important of the four demands formulated by the Liga association is for the government to recall a proposal for a health insurance reform and to present a new concept for a public discussion.
The second requirement is that a new way of counting pensions valid from next year is gradually introduced.
A third in order to ensure the possibility of inclusion in the system before 2010 for early retirement for the relevant fields of employment.
The fourth reason for the action is the fact that the Independent Trade Union of Railway Workers (VDSZSZA), which falls under the Liga trade association, does not accept an offer from the Ministry of Economy and Transport relating to railway branches, and awaits a different offer.
Political Capital: The Hungarian Guard has increased the risk of the country
According to the Risk Analysing Division (Risk Analyssing Division), the activities of the Hungarian Guard, founded with the support of Jobbik Magyarorgért in August this year, according to the Risk Analysing Division (Risk Analyssing Division), increased the political risk of Hungary and the entire region in several respects.
In connection with the activities of the Hungarian Guard, the greatest political risk poses the greatest political risk that "excurrence of already existing ethnic tensions between the Romani and non-Romani populations of Hungary may occur in a short period of time violent ethnic clashes".
The main reason is the fact that the political strategy of the Hungarian Guard is probably aimed at provoking such an action - supplied by a research institute.
As he writes, all this can be interpreted by one of the greatest negligenuties of Hungarian political leaders: "Public discussion on the Roma issue was left to representatives of radical and extremist political groupings, who could build a political strategy on the Roma-Hungarian contradiction."
This exacerbates the problem, impossess normal dialogue, strengthens extremists and increases the likelihood of violent conflicts - the institute judges.
In addition, the activities of the Hungarian Guard, according to the research institute, due to the great attention of domestic and foreign media, "to a large extent ruined the image of Hungary abroad, especially in terms of the belief in the stability of the country and its democratic maturity".
The institute recalls: part of the reorganization of Hungarian radical and far-right groups, which have been getting more and more publicity and vehemence since the autumn of 2006, is the fact that since the summer of 2007, several organizations have been created in Hungary, which are themselves called "National Militia".
"The common feature of these groupings is that they define themselves as civic associations, while they openly proclam the readiness of their members to perform def defensive tasks (in the event of natural disasters, invasion of the homeland, disruption of order), in addition, pointing to the incompetition of the police, the army, or the state," he adds.
Furthermore, he notes: all this is happening in a way that seeks to pack all sorts of political quests based on society’s opposition to politics and parties into civilian robes.
Emphasizing the civility and the form of the association, therefore, in the case of these groups, does not serve only to avoid the legal pituitual pitfalls of judicial registration, but it is also a political strategy.
According to the analysis, the activity of the Hungarian Guard is also a risk-encoming agent in terms of neighbourly relations.
"In recent months, they have been pointing to the Hungarian Guard in several neighbouring states as a potential source of danger, with ultra-Non-National political representatives of some neighboring countries want to acquain their own anti-Hungarian policies, by calling for the creation of the Hungarian Guard.
All this can have an impact on the political stability of the area," he adds.
According to the research institute, the formation of the Hungarian Guard in Central and Eastern Europe is not an isolated phenomenon, so the political risks to the area as a whole have increased.
As he writes, the activity of the Hungarian Guard resembles, for example, the activities of the Bulgarian National Guard, the creation of which was announced in August 2007 by the far-right Bulgarian National Union (BNU).
On the backdrop of the formation of the Bulgarian Guard stands mass Romani unsituations, which broke out in one of the Sofia districts (Krasna Poljana).
BNU took advantage of this to establish a guard, saying that the goal of the organization is a "national militia".
In the past 17 years there has been "Gypsy Terror in Bulgaria", but the state remained idle and indifferent.
He adds that the initiative provoked a turbulent discussion of the Bulgarian public.
As he writes, an increase in the risk of ethnic clashes signals an announcement by some Bulgarian Romani organizations to create their own garda as a sign of resistance.
Since the existing activity of the Hungarian Guard shows similarities with the activity of the Bulgarian National Guard, it is not excluded that even Hungarian Roma will respond to the threat in a similar way, by establishing their own militia, we can read in a warning about the risks drawn up by the institute Political Capital.
Attila Juhász, the research director of the Political Capital institute: risk analysis is one of the activities of a research institute.
As he said, the risk analysis is issued every year and if it finds something that could have an impact on the change of risk, they inform the public opinion, as in this case by issuing a risk warning.
Holidays are not free everywhere
In Hungary, the days of leave are precisely determined by the law and it has already become a general practice that working days are shifting around the holidays, which awaits us fewer times next year.
There are no unified festivities in the European Union.
The Hungarian legal system distinguishes national and public holidays and rest days.
The days of working rest are usually related to church holidays or important historical events.
In our country we also celebrate the new year: the last day of the old day and the first day of the new year is a day of work - on the New Year already so that people can take a rest after New Year's Eve.
During the time of the year we otherwise have a total of eleven vacancies.
The national feast is on March 15 celebrating the revolution of 1848 and October 23, commemorative day of the 1956 revolution.
On August 20, we celebrate the founding of the state, on May 1 work, on November 1 and on November 2 we reminisce about deceased relatives and friends.
In Addition, we have a two-day feast of Easter, Pentecostal and Christmas.
Since our national, national, or religious holidays are seldom per weekend according to the calendar, it has become the practice of shifting the working day in cases where we only work for one day before or after a free feast.
However, the price for long-term weekends is the fact that the previous Saturdays we stay in the workplace and at the school.
We have been deploring when the day Immediately recedues or following the festival, we have been working for many years, the Minister of Labor has been reguliled in a special ordinance.
The legal regulation applies equally to all employers and workers employed by them, to public servants as well as for persons in the public service.
However, it does not apply to companies and institutions that are uninterrupted without interruption or with regard to their determination also operate during rest days.
This year there will be a change in the working rules only around the holidays at the end of the year: from December 24, life in the country will almost stop, because, according to previous experience, the days between Christmas and New Year's Eve will "find work in advance" or thus take advantage of saved holidays.
In the next year, several of our holidays fall in the middle, respectively at the end of the week, so there will be fewer workday shifts than this this year.
For the first time, the calendar will turn around the feast of work, so that the workers can then stay at home for four days of taste.
Sabbath on April 26 will be a working day, on the contrary, it can be Friday, May 2, a day of rest.
Another move is related to the festivities on October 23: on Saturday, October 18 will work instead of Friday 24.
The end of the year, however, will be able to take place entirely under the sanctuary of holidays, because from December 24 they will have almost non-stop holidays, even though Silvestra falls on Wednesday.
