The Czech Republic has a Chance to earn 365 billion
Ministers of the Czech government yesterday signed a total of nine operational programmes with the representatives of the European Commission, of which the Czech Republic can receive 14 billion euros (approximately 365 billion crowns in the coming years).
It is about half of the total amount that the Czech Republic can receive from Brussels between 2007 and 2013.
Approximately 125 billion crowns will go from seven operational programs to the regions.
Czech companies will be able to obtain around CZK 100 billion from the Entrepreneurship and Innovation program.
Most money, up to $150 billion, will go into transport.
The transport program is the largest operational program and represents up to 22 percent of the funds that the Czech Republic can receive from funds.
This money will increase the budget of the State Fund for Transport Infrastructure, which will manage CZK 90.8 billion next year.
The Entrepreneurship and Innovation program is intended for entrepreneurs and companies to raise funds for innovative entrepreneurship.
Firestrians should raise funds for the introduction of new technologies, for industrial research, as well as for introducing more efficient organizational methods.
In the current drawing of money from EU funds, the Czech Republic ranks among the least successful within the newly recruited countries.
