The driver's license didn't have to be exchanged 600 thousand people
Six-hundred- Thousand drivers missed the deadline and didn't manage to exchange an old driver's license that expires at the end of the year.
Today it is the last day when people can apply for an exchange, so that the authorities still manage to issue a new card for them by the end of the year.
However, the ministry is not afraid that hundreds of thousands of drivers will travel on the road after the New Year without a valid authorization.
According to the authorities, those who don’t even want to drive no longer have exchanged the card.
While municipalities report a sharp decrease in interest in the replacement of the driver's license, the authorities in the metropolis are overwhelmed and the interest in exchanging the licence has risen this week.
The magistrate handles around 2000 clients a day.
We've been waiting in queues for about half an hour.
Approximately 140,000 drivers did not change their driving licence in Prague.
Exhibition of a new card lasts twenty days.
However, it is possible to apply for extradition within a shortened period of five days.
In this case, the driver will pay five hundred crowns.
Motorists who do not manage to replace the licence by the end of the year and go out on the road without a valid driver's license will face a fine from January.
The offender will pay a maximum of two thousand kroners.
However, the policeman can also deal with the offense by an agreement.
In the event of an administrative misdemeallenfaction, the fine will amount to CZK 2500.
