More than one pregnancies out of three (36%) are still unexpanded today, according to a study led by the French Institute national d'études demographiques (Ined) - the State Institute of Demographic Studies, forty years after the adoption of the so-called Neuwirth law, which enacted contraception in France.
This conceivation includes unintentional pregnancies (24%), as well as misinterpreted or unexplained in an unexpected manner.
