Reverteenable Repliability of the Space Station
More than seven hours of work in space was needed by astronaut Scott Parazynski and members of his crew from the International Space Station (ISS) to reconsider a thrifted solar panel, necessary for the station's further scientific activity.
It was a risky ascension into the universe, which scorched records in terms of duration, the distance from residential modules, the velocity with which it was projected and the rates of "go-roundhood" that the astronauts spent on the repair.
Difficulty emerged on Tuesday, while the astronauts from Discovery unleash module Harmony, a large cylindrical formation designed to install the European and Japanese scientific laboratories (see frame).
This module is a kind of lander for modules-Laboratories.
However, it is necessary to be able to supply them with electricity.
Therefore, the crew's second task was to relocate a seventeen-and-a-hundred-ton module producing electricity using solar panels, which was already located on the ISS, so that it anchored at its final habitat.
After relocating it, the crew began dismantling sixty-seven-metre-metre-long solar panels of the module.
And in this, one of the panels, disintegrating as a pulling harmonica, as a result of pinning the cable, was damaged on an area of less than one meter.
Disintegration has been paused in order to prevent further damage to the panel.
Astronauts, who were originally supposed to carry out a control output to the Discovery ship, and then go to repair another solar panel whose rotation system had a malay, were compelled to devote themselves to a damaged panel.
And it was Scott Parazynski who had been chosen to go at the end of the ship's robotic arm added to the station's arm, and carried out a repair.
It's one of the best "spacewalkers" (senior pedestrians) of the U.S. Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA).
Tall, sturdy, very agile, has a very crafted chest and long arms.
At the age of 46, the doctor was tasked with "operating" the "surrected" solar panel.
After researching the damages in detail, he cut off the defective cable and fixed to the damaged places a kind of "quiggles".
He was assisted by a second "spacewalker", which remained near the crucifixion, and also from the inside, other astronauts, among them Peggy Witson, the crew commander.
The tools he'd-appoints he'd-cimerating-finger-cream-glue-lapped to prevent electroshock on solar panels producing several hundred volts were invented, and "under-thules" were made by astronauts aboard the station.
At the end of the scheduling, Scott Parazynski awaited the panel unlaunchably undisclosed and then invented his tools and went back to the inner part of the station.
Yesterday in the afternoon, the astronauts enjoyed a six-day rest before today, when seven astronauts are returning to the Discovery ship to return to Earth on Wednesday as it is planned.
EADS shares are weakening
EADS shares are ablindrically disappearing on the Paris Stock Exchange, after the company operating in the aeronautical and defense industries announced that it would have to spend €2.4 billion in order to face an A400M lag.
EADS has lost 4% and is now at €21.96 on the Paris Stock Exchange.
The financial group was compelled to reconsider its projected production results for 2007 as a result of devastation resulting from slow advance progress in the development of the A400M engine, which is a precondition for an inaugural flight.
The price for easing delays in the delivery of a military lorry, announced in October, was quantified "up to €1.4 billion, more than a billion for Airbus," the EADS maternity company announced.
Due to these costs, EADS, next Thursday, at the presentation of its quarterly results, will be forced to announce a new profit outlook for interest and taxes (EBIT).
The group also revealed that the new cost estimate corresponds to a six-per-month delay.
Recacall that EADS production results in 2006 fell 86%, mainly due to the costs associated with the delay of another program, the giant A380.
Originally, the group predicted that it would provide the first A400M van to the French army in October 2009.
Judgment for quo status quo
Sunday's elections will take place unattaulied expectations: the Russians will majorityly elect the party of President Putin, United Russia.
Conceivably, after the end of a very low-free election campaign, its gravity towards stability, even for authoritarianism.
Today, three days before the elections to the Chamber of Deputies, Russian President Vladimir Putin will communicate a pre-retrievable televised message to the electorate on public broadcasters, the content of which, however, is kept secret.
He does so from the position of the leader of United Russia, the pro-Kremlin party, which seems to be celebrating a crushing victory.
When the ambassadors of foreign states were accepting yesterday, the president did not let anything come out of him and was satisfied with another attack on the West accused of interfering - his favorite theme during the Campaign.
"We are aware of the award of true democracy and we want an honest, most transparent and open-minded choice, elections without the slightest flaw in beauty," he added.
In the eyes of the Opposition, this is not nearly the case.
Convict the campaign marked by various coercive pressures.
Communist leader Gennady Zyuganov says that "never avoided such filthy elections, even for Yeltsin".
After repressions accompanying last weekend's demonstration, former world chess champion Garry Kasparov, was sentenced to five days in prison for an illicit demonstration.
"The Russians have left the mentality homo sovietica"
In the background of this parliamentary election of simple tensile anticipation, two far-opener questions are profiled:
"Who becomes Putin's successor in the presidency?
An official newspaper yesterday published the date of the first round of the presidential election, March 2, 2008; nominees can present themselves to the public until December 23.
Vladimir Putin, who was elected in 2000 and re-equivoted in 2004, cannot seek a third mandate in a row.
However, there is no successor.
"What role will Putin play after March?"
He's going to be a prime minister?
“Cretell of a parliamentary majority and an almighty United Russia party that chooses a government and the president?
In one way or another, an outgoing ruling power will triumph on the whole line in the parliamentary, as well as in the presidential elections.
It's a tradition.
“The Russians have remained the mentality of homo sovietica, they do not feel the masters of their destiny,” said sociologist Lev Gudkov, director of an independent Levada center.
Historian Nikolai Kopossov from the State University of Sankt-Peterburg notices a more distant context: civil society has gained, in this country rescheduled five centuries after Europe; the glorious commemororative spirit delayed the formation of individualism.
“Putin followed the pat-nationist model of the state, perfectly accepted by the population, all the more so because this new paternalism did not accompany terror, but a certain economic well-being”, believes Maria Lipman of the Carnegie Foundation.
The Russians today "voluntarily renounce personal responsibilities", which they briefly demonstrated after the collapse of the USSR.
"Why to think about it?"
This phenomenon applies to all strategments, including the business world.
Even the clerical elite intends to maintain quo status quo: 65 governors (out of a total of 85 heads of the Russian regions) are run by the local candidates of United Russia.
As in the 1990s, new liberties taken from the West are often synonymous with chaos.
Public opinion favors stability.
Likewise, in the name of stability, the Russians won't vote for extremists.
Conclusion Tamara Čeredničenko, a fifty-four-year-old professor: "Why to think?
Those in power aren’t that bad, so why change them?”
Difficulty memory
After more than sixty years in an intimate regime, the Nazi archives from Bad Arolsen, retrieving the fate of 17.5 million casualties of the Hitler Regime, are being opened to the public.
47 million archival documents deposited in the length of 27 km in Bad Arolsen (Hesse) had until this time been accessible only for the "humanitarian" purpose, i.e. individually and nominally, at the request of a former victim or his authorized persons.
Eleven states tasked with managing archives - among which Germany, France, Israel and the United States - agreed in May to open them to scientists and historians.
Since the ratification process of this agreement by all states is over, the opening came into effect yesterday.
Sensitive information
The free approach of historians to Bad Arolsen will make it possible to investigate "particularly the movements of inmates, the populations of the camps and the state of forcibly workers", explains Reto Meistern, director of these archives governed by the International Committee of the Red Precifight (Comité international de la Croix-rouge, CICR).
Until recently, there have been several states, among them Germany, against making these nominal documents available to the public because of the sensible nature of some information.
What are the expected homosexuality or the mental affiliation of certain victims of deportation.
Registries of concentration camps or arrest warrants compiled by the Gestapo were assembled after the aftermath after the war for the practical purpose of finding deported or forced labour subjugated by civilians, bringing them proof of their insternation in order to open the path of their compensation.
Even today, more than 300 perpetrators in Bad Arolsen deal with tens of thousands of individual applications.
However, access to Bad Arolsen poses only a limited benefit for part of the scientific community.
“From these documents, nothing fundamentally new can be expected,” Wolfgang Benz, Director of the Centre for Anti-Semitism in Berlin’s Technische Universität said in 2006.
The EU and India to Achieve a Free Trade Agreement in 2008
Bilateral trade between Europe and India currently stands at nearly €60 billion a year.
The EU is India's first trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign commerce.
The European Union and India await the signing of a free-traffic treaty in 2008, European Trade Commissioner Peter Mandelson and his Indian counterpart Kamal Nath.
In April of last year, EU foreign ministers gave the green light to the European Commission to start negotiations to sign free trade treaties (accords de libre échange, ALE) with India, South Korea and the Southeast Asian (Asean). Bilateral trade between Europe-India already amounts to nearly €60 billion a year.
The EU is India's first trading partner and accounts for 18% of its foreign trade.
The EU is also its first foreign investor, but according to the European Commission, India is the ninth trading partner of the EU.
“The free-traffigment agreement tremendously diverts both economies” and “India will gain better access to the 450-million-strength thriving Europeans,” Peter Mandelson said.
Europe represents the first or the second market for each of the top ten products exported by India, the European commissioner clarified. The Asian and European giant together annually exchanged "47 billion euros into goods" and "ten billion euros in services", Danièle Smadja, the head of the European Commission's Delegation in New Delhi, regretting that the bilateral trade "has not yet achieved its full potential."
(Source of AFP)
The Bank of England took note of concerns and offered £10 billion in a five-week Auction
The Bank of England announced on Thursday that it intends to alleviate current fears of deteriorating conditions on the credit market again and announ an £10bn bid in a five-week auction at a base interest rate of 5.75%, an offer valid unusually long.
“In an effort to make it easier for fears, according to which conditions in the financial markets will be very unfavourable at the end of the year and to give the banks greater certainty in the way to secure its cash position for this period, the Bank intends to offer a significant part of its planned reserve during the maintenance period, which will begin on December 6 in the form of a five-week open-market operation.”
The bank specifies that £10 billion (EUR 14 billion) will thus be placed on the financial market on December 6 at 12.15 GMT until January 10, at a base interest rate.
Seems like it's the first-ever BAE is pumping cash into the financial market in a five-week open-to-market operation.
It normally lasts a week.
BOE adds in its communiqué that "remains ready to carry out additional measures to maintain interest rates on an online rate" of inter-bank lending at the same level at its basic rate.
Inter-Bank interest rate was 5,829% on Wednesday.
The three-month interest rate settled at 6.6%, the highest figure since September 18.
From the beginning of the summer financial crisis, the sums placed on the financial market by the English bank associated with fee rates that have discouraged banks from using this offer.
According to certain speculations strengthened by the development of the pound's exchange rate against the euro, many preferred to opt for sums placed on the financial market by the European Central Bank with lower rates and more guaranteed discretion.
UMP (Union pour mouvement populaire, Union for People's Movements) and NC (Nouveau Centre (Nouveau Centre) Refuse to Address Socialists (PS) Proposals on Purchasing Competitiveness
UMP and Nouveau Centre clubs on Thursday declined to discuss the individual paragraphs of the Socialist bill on purchases, which is equivalent to rejecting the text.
On the agenda, the text of the bill came within the so-called socialist "nesnest" (a meeting initiated by an individual parliamentary club) and contained a dozen measures taken on Tuesday by the chairmanship of the PS, among which there was an increase in the employment premium by 50 %, the resumption of fluctuating TIPPs, transport cheque or rent regulation.
Given the fact that the UMP and NC voted against the discussion of individual paragraphs (180 votes against 115), the meeting was ended after a general debate, which became an opportunity for an opinion exchange, sometimes more vivid, between the majority and the opposition, a few hours before Nicolas Sarkozy's televised appearance on the purchase.
Jean-Marc Ayrault, the head of parliament, has announced that his club will resubmit these proposals in their entirety in the form of additions to an amendment to the Finance Bill, which the Chamber of Deputies will be debated next week.
A new festival is being reasurrected
As a result of many speculations that C3 Presents is launching a new festival in Filadelphia, this promoteor/producer Vineland Festival in New Jersey, in collaboration with the Republic Festival of the Republic, announced British organizer Melvin Benn.
“It is an honor for our company to work with a person who without exaggeration has inspired the current festival movement in America,” Charlie Jones of C3 told Billboard.com.
C3 produces the Chicago festival Lollapalooza and the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Vineland in New Jersey is a summer target campsite.
The festival should take place from August 8 to August 10 on a private 500-acre farm, about a 40-minute time since Philadelphia.
The director of the Republic festival, formerly known as Mean Fiddler, one of the world's most acquainted festival organizers.
In 1989 he took the rudder of the Reading Festival in the United Kingdom, which attracts 80 000 people every year.
In 1999 Melvin Benn added the Leeds Festival to his Portfolio Portfolio. In 2006, Festival Republic founded the Latitude Festival at Henham Park in Suffolk.
Starting in 2002, Melvin Benn as a co-owner is also in charge of producing, licenses and organizing tasks at the Glastonbury Festival, which today has a capacity of up to 177,500.
C3 Charlie Jones calls Glastonbury a "most inspirational event" ever experienced and says his firm and Melvina Benna are working at the same time to put a European-style festival event for the region.
“Originally we chose Philadelphia as a market, and together with the Fairmount Parks Commission, we worked hard to set up a festival in the center of Philadelphia,” says Charlie Jones.
“We negotiated with the city and the Commission was motivated and enthusiastic about the project.
Unfortunately, due to the current leadership of the city, we got bogged down in politicking, adds Charlie Jones.
"Fortunately, we had the opportunity to discuss with Melvin Benn and we are going to start a great festival in an exceptional place, which will ultimately serve the inhabitants of Philadelphia."
C3 Presents resurredited the Lollapalooza festival in Grant Park, Chaga, in 2005, after they excelled at the Austin City Limits of the Music Festival in 2002.
Coarse repercussion of both events for 2007 amounted to 9,8M$ and 11.3M.
Both of these festivals take place in an urban environment.
Melvin Benn’s European model takes place in the countryside, while our festivals take place more in green spaces in the cities,” says Charlie Jones.
Our goal is to reconcile both concepts in a certain way in order to create both the impression of a rural festival after Europe and the city-centicurse.”
Vineland is located about halfway between Philadelphia and Atlantic City.
"Vineland, including the mayor, enthusiastically supports the realization of the event," says Charlie Jones.
The latter refuses to divuve the terms of the agreement, but he argues "that they are advantageous enough to make it possible to invest in such an event and to welcome the festival it will have, hopefully, a long-lasting time".
Charlie Jones says the festival's capacity is "very very high," similar to Bonnaroo Music Festival in the Tennessee Bonnaroo Music Festival that accommodates 80,000 people.
He says that the groups have already received invitations, but nothing can yet be reconsidered when the program is just put into the press.
"Vineland will have a rock tinge, but the musoy will be colorful for us to attract a wide range of spectators as much as possible," says Carlie Jones.
C3, which won the Top Independent Promoter award in the last Billboard Touring Awards are Charlie Walker and Charles Attal.
