We've done it.
With this phrase, Paolo Vasile, executive chairman Telecinco, expressed his gratification at the end of trading, when he stated that the television he was driving doubled the value of its rival Antena 3.
Only one thing ruined his joy: 'what I'm sorry is that it didn''t happen because we'd rise more, but because we've fallen less,' he said.
At the same time, he stressed that, thanks to the weak market, 'we fell less'.
Telecinco ended trading by 2.54/4 %.
This profit shifted their loss for the past part of the year to 15.66%.
According to Bloomberg, the stock exchange value of this mediaset-dominated firm (52% capital) with Vocent (nexThurs 13%) reaches €448.88 million, according to Bloomberg data.
Its competitor Antena 3, which fell 1.52% yesterday and has fallen by 40.5% overall since January, having half the value of 2 193.46 million.
The value of other telecommunications companies that have been valued is 3,571 billion for Sogecable, 2 518.53 million Prisa (Cinco Días) and 1.779 billion Vocento.
According to Vasile, the comparison with Antena 3 is being offered because we are talking about two similar companies.
Relative fact is how much we are able to do in the same market, at what cost and how we evaluate it in viewership.
Telencinuco announced last week that this year it envisages surviving billions of coarse advertising revenue will become the first television channel, as assured by Giuseppe Tringali, executive chairman Telecinco and Publiespaña, a branch that advertises the group.
If predicted data were actually obtained, this TV channel would see an increase in a 3.6/8 per cent revenue increase this year, compared to 965.4 million in 2006.
At the same time in the first nine months of the year, Antena's net turnover increased by 1.6 per cent (accompanied $734.4 million), while television's net revenue increased by 0.7% ($630.4 million).
One of the factors that analysts are focused on for the best relative development of Telecinco on the stock exchange is an increased pay out, which it has retained so far: in 2006, this firm, chaired Alejandro Echevarría, distributed 100 per cent of its profits among its shareholders.
Vasile reassures that although it’s too early to make a decision, this coefficient could be changed after the purchase of 33% of Endemol together with its parent company Mediaset.
"We have an official commitment to give at least 50%, although we have always reported much more.
This year, I hope that we will be able to gratify our shareholders, with whom we have already increased the value of 33 % of Endemol'.
According to analysts, the market shows some fatigue in these moments.
Lehman Brothers recently downgraded Telecincico's earnings estimates, 4% in 2008 and 7% in 2009.
This is according to this, explaining that projected revenue growth from 0.5% to 8.4 per cent in 2008 halted and 5.5% to 5.1% in 2009.
The so-to-deficit company reduced Antena 3’s expected profit, 4.5% in 2008 and 7.5% in 2009.
3 opinions
1.
Ibersecurities: Required to purchase both titles primarily based on an increased dividend yield and long-term sustainable potential.
2.
Caja Madrid: rated better Telecinco (huge) than Antenu 3 (maintained) due to its 'numerary advantages' and the growth of trade.
3.
JPMorgan: in both cases he recommends not to overestimate them because it faces 'similar threats' (oversatisfied market and deteriorated economic environment).
The Congress Appriased MiFID Trans-Invalidation Valid from November 1
Simultaneously with parliamentary talks, which were concluded today by a congressional vote on amendments incorporated by the Senate into the bill, the government underwent a public hearing an order that develops a new law, in order for both to come into force before the end of the year.
Representatives of each party congruently emphasized the efforts of deputies and senators to nenegotiable and to agree on the best standard in order to guarantee the protection of investors and adequate regulation of the activities of entities necessary for the effective functioning of the markets.
The MiFID Directive, which governs the Act on Securities, envisage modernization of financial markets and at the same time strengthens the protection of the investor, improves the supervisory powers of the State Commission for the Securities market (CNMV) and promotes cooperation between the various supervisory authorities of the European Union.
This new regulation will make it possible to provide financial advisory services to both specialised firms and natural or legal persons to create a new type of financial service firms (ESIS), financial advisory firms (AFIs) that join securities companies, securities intermediary offices and portfolio management companies.
In Addition, the number of systems for the performance of financial-in-equiry operations is being expanded in such a way that multifaceted trading systems and command internalisation systems that will compete with simultaneous bur-sectoral brokers are being added.
Furthermore, the law obliges companies providing investment services on the market to disseminate information about the key aspects of their business profile, risk-taking risks and ways of coping with the risk, and requires keeping a statement of all completed operations to simplify supervision by CNMV.
During the discussion in the Congressional Trade Commission, several adjustments were included, among which stands out that securitiated receivables were considered a "comprehensible" financial instrument given the high-hazard of the investor that has been demonstrated by what happened in the U.S. with high-risk mortgage debt (subprime).
In addition, the transposition of the directive has been used to lawfully decompose functions that can be held by bachelors in economics and business management 30 years after the Royal Decree has been approved in 1977, which sets out professional functions reserved for economists.
At the same time, the senate included the creation of new professions in the financial sector, such as an intermediary that will work externally, it will not require permission from the CNMV and will be able to provide product trading services and acquiring clients for various investment firms at the same time.
Harmonized ISSC increased by five-tenth to 4.1% in November
This indicator, which is later assisted by Eurostat for the calculation of the European Union's inflation index, provides preliminary information on how prices have evolved in Spain during the month of November.
Its publication corresponds to the policy of Eurostat and the Central European Bank (CEB) to provide data over time and quality comparable to those achieved in the United States.
This predicated indicator is calculated using the same process that is used for the Harmonised Index of Consumer Prices, but using different statistical modelling methods for estimating information that is still unavailable at the time of publication.
The Spanish INE (State Institute for Statistics) recalled that the information provided by this preliminary indicator is only indicative and therefore does not necessarily coincide with the final data, which will come into acquaintance on December 14 this year.
"ISC will continue to maintain at a relatively high level"
Deputy Prime Minister and Economy Minister Pedro Solbes said the ISC's January increase to 4.1% in November is "commnending", but at the same time he predicted that the price index will continue to be at a relatively "high level" in the coming months.
In any case, Solbes clarified that "even if it is not a favorable number", Spain's inflation differentiation to the monetary union over the past two years is "more or less".
He also explained that November "was less surprising" than the previous month, when the government did not expect such a high increase.
"We expected a value of around 4%," the Minister of the Economy said.
Virgin plans to $42 Billion with Northern Rock in three years
Since Northern Rock went into crisis in mid-September and had to resort to an emergency loan from the Bank of England, its deposits have plummeted by more than 50 per cent to £12 billion ($16.8 billion).
At the time, the bank managed record deposits worth more than £25 Billion, which gradually declined over two-and-and-a-hal-month unconfidence months, even though the government offered a one-hundred-percent guarantee for this money and prolong it until the end of the crisis.
The company Virgin, which will replace an entity's name with its trademark Virgin Money, needs about a quarter of revenues deposited into British banks over the next three years to earn the remaining £18 billion, reaching a $30 billion target.
Magnat Richard Branson, known in the United Kingdom with its conspicuous advertising campaigns, plans to spend £50 million (approximately €70 million) a year on advertising and marketing to achieve its resolution.
The Northern Rock bank this week marked the offer of the Virgin consortium, which consists of three other companies, such as the one that prefers to save them from bankruptcy.
