Mayor and local police chief Totana detained on suspicion of corruption practices during construction
As the investigative sources reported, the Civil Guard arrested the mayor of the Murcia town of Totan, the "popularist" José Martínez Andreo, the head of the local police, the secretor of the town hall and a businesswoman in the hospitality, on the suspicion of committing crimes during the construction.
The mayor has been arrested in his residence and transported to the town hall, in whose premises he is now located along with a number of police officers, who have also appeared at the Construction Commission and the Municipal Enterprise for the Management of Industrial Lands and Apartments.
These three arrests were added to six, which took place last Monday in Galicia, Murcia and Madrid, in an operation related to reclassification of more than 2 million hectares of agricultural land on land suitable for the built-up area, that Galician firm Nuaria, after paying illicit commissions during the previous parliamentary term, could have built 4,000 homes.
In addition, the other two persons were not under arrest, but are charged in an abbreviated proceeding in the Court of First Instance of Totana.
The top six arrested were handed over to the court today.
According to information sources, the previous mayor of Totany is being investigated and now a member of the Autonomous Parliament for the People's Party (PP), Juan Morales.
Furthermore, his ex-wife, the owner of the real estate agency registered in Totana, was also charged with his current girlfriend living in Murcia, the capital of an Autonomous region.
Manuel N.A., the director and owner of the Nuaria group, a lawyer and businessman from Vigo, has been accumulating in Nigran (Pantevedra province), as well as Pablo José M. G., director of Suelo de Inmonuar, belonging to that group and through which briberies were handed over.
Investigations are carried out by a group for offences in the construction of an operational central unit of the Civil Guard, whose members, in addition to the arrest, have also carried out eleven searches, mostly in companies related to those arrested, based in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontever, Las Rozas (comination of Madrid) and Tothana.
Only one person was imprisoned in Totanna at that time, a very well-familiar business owner for poultrymeat products, who could serve as an intermediary.
Nuaria Group was tasked with erculpating the largest residency complex of the Murcia city of Totany, which would represent the construction of more than 5,000 houses, a golf course and two "spa hotels".
In Tothana, the company acquired 2.2 square meters of land, which was reclassified and its project was intended to double the settlement of the municipality, which has a population of 25,000 inhabitants.
Nuaria Group consists of companies such as Autesa and Inomunar, which are dedicated to supporting the real estate market, Conycase, which manages parking on the streets of Coruña, Venezuela and Fernando el Católico Square in Vigo, Hogartel dedicated to direct marketing and Preconiza, which focuses on the propagation, sale and installation of building elements.
