Von Beust rehearses criticism for renouncing Olympics
The mayor's resignation from the hosting of the Summer Olympic Games in Hamburg has come across sharp criticism from politics and economics.
Many still want to fight for the arrangement of games by the water.
Von Beust urges realism in estimating chances.
The chief conductor of the Chamber of Commerce in Hamburg, Hans-Jörg Schmidt-Trenz, on Wednesday described this decision "unfortunate in terms of entrepreneurship".
No other project has recently awakened such a great motivation in the city as an Olympic idea.
"Without this goal, it wouldn't be possible to maintain this sport-political enthusiasm at such a high degree."
Schmidt-Trenz urged the Senate not to bury this project, but to create a new long-term concept "which is based on an altered time schedule."
Mayor Ole von Beust remained with his earlier testimonies on Wednesday, according to Hamburg's Olympic ambitions until at least 2028, unrealistic.
"Not Hamburg, but the German Olympic Sports Association will decide the Olympic candidacy", von Beust told the newspaper WELT ONLINE.
He pointed out that at the beginning of December the Sports Association will decide Munich's candidacy for winter games in 2018.
"This preference for us means we don't have a realistic chance with the 2028 timetable."
Nevertheless, this dream has not yet come to an end, von Beust said.
The Hamburg Sports Association (HSB) called von Beust's remarks regrettable.
It gives the impression that Hamburg does not want to compete for the Olympic Games over the next twenty-five years.
"It's still too soon to ruin a chance by calling the plans buried at this early stage," HSB President Günter Ploss said on Wednesday.
Reluctuation would be inconsistent with the testimonies of the head of the senate he uttered at the general meeting of the General German University Sports Association.
Von Beust did not announce the candidacy of Hamburg for the University in 2015 as a replacement for organizing the Olympic Games.
In the past week it has just been nominated for a candidate town.
The SPD faction has rebuildrically blamed the Senate for wasting a valuable time that could be exploited for the construction of apartments in Hamburg.
"The development of the Klein Grasbrook area has been hindered by the Senate for years because they bet on hosting the Olympics and expelled the construction of apartments," SPD deputies Carola Veit and Jan Quast said.
While SPD for the Klein Grasbrook area was still planning an Olympics, saying the entire area would later be used for housing purposes, the CDU unanimously relied on an "Olympic factor".
Applauasing for the Summer Olympics in 2012 at its time provoked a lot of enthusiasm in Hamburg.
But Hamburg crashed in Leipzig.
These aren't Warhol boxes
The one who associates the terms Sweden and the wooden crates does not think about Andy Warhol, but on Ikea.
Isn't it?
Wooden crates currently produced in Sweden cast dark shadows on the list of Warhol's works.
Most of him on the list of ninety-four "Brillo boxes" such as Stockholm are falsifiers.
A few months ago, the Swedish newspaper "Expressen" expressed doubts about the authenticity of Warhol's "Brillo boxes" from 1968, an in-house research of the Moderna Museetus museum in Stockholm with a result that brought disillusions; six "Brillo boxes", which was donated by its former director Pontus Hulten in 1995, are copies - as well as the majority of the "Brillo boxes" of Stockholm.
Prevulnerable events are a tangled, confusing chain of artistic and curating events.
Warhol produced his first Brillo boxes in New York in 1964, painting wooden crayons, which were based on the red-and-blue-and-and-white Brill soap powder boxes.
An exhibition of his works at Moderna Museet in 1968 - with Warhol's endorsement - demonstrated hundreds of Brillo crazes from a carton. These did not come (for financial reasons) from Warhol, but were supplied directly from the Brillo factory.
It wasn't the works of art, it wasn't about the works of art, it's mere exhibition pieces.
Warhol probably also gave permission in 1968 to produce several wooden brills in Sweden, but they are not exhibited at Moderna Museet.
Witnesses at that time are now talking about fifteen crayons, which at that time rightly went into artistic and auction history as authorized originals - "Andy Warhol's Brillo Boxes" with the designation Typ Stockholm.
Some of them at auctions were auctioned for more than $100 000.
The problem now arises in the fact that Pontus Hutén's legendary director later falsely argued that approximately a hundred crates were produced and exhibited in Sweden in 1968, which Warhol then left him.
In fact, 105 Hulten crates were produced in Malmö for an exhibition in St. Petersburg only in 1990.
At that time Warhol was dead three years.
Lars Byström, the top conservator Moderna Museet, explored, in addition to six Brill boxes owned by the museum, as well as three Brillo boxes from the Swedish private collection, two of which were made in Sweden in 1968 and after their plycloth slabs were coarse-painted with basic paint and abraded, they were rubbed with an oil-white paint.
On the contrary, it emerged from the structure of copies from 1990 that the paint had been applied with a painting role directly on the plywood plate without the previous prime of paint - in addition, it is an acrylic and not an oily paint.
"These crates have not been authorized by the artist and should be eliminated from Warhol's official Deed Brill Boxes," said Lars Nittve, Director of Moderna Museet: "Whether Andy Warhol Art Authentication Board in New York doesn't collurate other conclusions, Moderna Museet will have to classify six crates of its exhibition collections as "exhibition - copies."
Already in July, Authentication Board announced that it will deal with these "protruding accusations" that had been brought about in the case of soap-cooked boxes.
However, the organization still persists in relentless silence.
Reselective Soldiers in Manila
Rebellious soldiers who for fortified themselves at a hotel in Manila have surrendered and demand the resignation of President Gloria Macapagal Arroy.
Insurgent commander Antonio Trillanes reproached the president for manipulating and corruption during the election, told reporters at the hotel that he denies responsibility for the bloodshed.
Soldiers devoted to the government had previously attacked a hotel with the deployment of tear gas.
A few hours earlier, about two dozen soldiers for fortified themselves in the building.
On Thursday, about half of them went on trial due to a thwarted coup attempt in 2003, including Trillates.
He took advantage of the meeting to fugitude with about 30 sympathizers.
Militants who were supposed to babysit him apparently defected to his side and joined the rebellion.
They broke into the Peninsula and demanded the resignation of Gloria Macapagal Arroy.
The government's loyal units closed the area around the selected hotel.
The president convened an urgent session of the security Cabinet.
National Security Adviser Norberto Gonzales denounced the demeasures.
"People have had enough," Triallnes said.
"We call on people to join us."
General Danilo Lim, the commander-in-chief of the former elite Scout Rangers unit, said other military units will join the march in a short period of time.
Critics of the government have called for a major demonstration to take place against the president on Friday.
Corruption has been reproaminated for months.
Maniland's financial region in 2003 became the main scene of a rebellion of about 200 troops against Arroy.
Because the army refused to join the insurgents, the rebellion crashed after less than 24 hours.
They have tried to overthroate a democratically elected government in the Philippines since 1986 at least seven times.
